    "source": "https://build.protomaps.com/20261014.pmtiles",
    "note": "Q790118/way240141751 identifies the main temple. Nine pinned standard PMTiles records fix the main mound, upper sanctuary and entrance part, four cruciform outer pavilions, eastern gopura and long cross-shaped causeway. Raw +X east and +Z south at heading0 retain its slight mapped axis rotation; the east entrance/causeway resolves the facing direction. Bayon to the southeast, Phimeanakas to the north and the Terrace of the Elephants east/northeast remain independent. Reused unmodified nearby N0497 Bayon standard PMTiles/Mapzen extract. Main terrace foundations and outer pavilions extend into the native terrain; the causeway deck is segmented along the coarse native ground with supports seated at each segment. This intentionally accommodates the noisy standard DEM rather than claiming surveyed level causeway elevations. Ground and mapped water remain native; no ground or water cutout. Preview uses the host terrain sample at the authored base; ground slope, facade azimuth and final site fit remain review items."
